  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.2 — Wire format fix\n• Fixed binary Protobuf serialisation — rewrote OtlpProto.cs with manual varint\n  encoding, replacing CodedOutputStream API which produced incorrect wire format\n  (\"wrong wireType = 0 for field SeverityText\" on export to all backends)\n• Removed Google.Protobuf dependency — only OpenTelemetry.Extensions.Hosting remains\n• All backends now receive correctly encoded OTLP Protobuf log records\nSee full changelog: https://github.com/SinkSharp/CHANGELOG.md\n\nv1.0.1 — Dependency updates\n• OpenTelemetry.Extensions.Hosting updated from 1.9.0 to 1.20.1\nSee full changelog: https://github.com/SinkSharp/CHANGELOG.md\n\nv1.0.0 — Initial release\n• True binary Protobuf export — gRPC (port 4317) and HTTP/Protobuf (port 4318)\n• Wire format implemented from scratch using manual varint encoding — no Google.Protobuf or third-party proto package\n• PII masking runs in-process before any OTLP write — CorrelationId, UserId, RequestPath, ElapsedMs on every log record\n• LogEvent → OTel LogRecord mapping per OTel Log Data Model spec: SeverityNumber, SeverityText, Body, log.record.original, code.namespace, correlation.id, trace.id, span.id, exception.type/message/stacktrace\n• Batching with configurable BatchSize (default 512) and FlushInterval (default 5s)\n• Error and Critical events flush immediately — never held in the batch\n• Retry with exponential back-off (1s → 2s → 4s) on transient failures\n• Graceful drain on shutdown — DisposeAsync flushes remaining buffer before exit\n• OtlpSuppressingHandler — prevents AddHttpClientInstrumentation from creating child spans for the sink's own OTLP export calls\n• AddSinkSharpTracing() — distributed tracing registration via configureTracing callback\n• Supported backends: Jaeger, Grafana/Loki, Datadog, New Relic, Honeycomb, Azure Monitor, any OTel Collector\nSee full changelog: https://github.com/SinkSharp/CHANGELOG.md",
